{"name":"Parasol","hex":"#e9dfde","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"parasol","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small light umbrella used as protection from the sun.","A miniature paper umbrella used as a decoration in tropical-themed cocktails."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To protect with, or as if with, a parasol; to shade."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parasol"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parasol (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Parasol (1800–1826) was a British Thoroughbred racehorse. In total she won twenty of her thirty-five races, including two Newmarket First October King's Plates, the Jockey-Club Plate and a match race against Derby winner Cardinal Beaufort. Her only race away from Newmarket was for her début, in the Oaks Stakes in 1803. She was bred and owned by Augustus FitzRoy, 3rd Duke of Grafton. As a broodmare she foaled the stallion Partisan, 2000 Guineas winner Pindarrie and Pastille, who won both the 2000 Guineas and the Oaks."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e9/Parasol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parasol_(horse)","wikidata":"Q17013446"},{"title":"Umbrella","blocks":[{"text":"An umbrella is a folding canopy supported by wooden or metal ribs that is mounted on a wooden, metal, or plastic pole. It is usually designed to protect a person against sun or rain. Initially, they were used in warmer countries for shade from the sun, but later evolved to also be used for protection from rain. Etymologically, the term umbrella is to be used when protecting from the sun, but is also commonly used when protecting from rain. Some countries specifically use the words parasol and parapluie to differentiate based on their use. There are also combinations of parasol and parapluie that are called en-tout-cas. A modern hand-held umbrella or parasol may have a black exterior canopy and a silver inner coating, for better protection from both the sun and ultraviolet rays, and may be water-resistant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/M0354_000727-005_1.jpg/330px-M0354_000727-005_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umbrella","wikidata":"Q41607"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Augustus_Henry_Fitzroy%2C_3rd_Duke_of_Grafton.jpg/500px-Augustus_Henry_Fitzroy%2C_3rd_Duke_of_Grafton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Augustus_Henry_Fitzroy%2C_3rd_Duke_of_Grafton.jpg/1280px-Augustus_Henry_Fitzroy%2C_3rd_Duke_of_Grafton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Augustus_Henry_Fitzroy%2C_3rd_Duke_of_Grafton.jpg/500px-Augustus_Henry_Fitzroy%2C_3rd_Duke_of_Grafton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Parasol's owner, the 3rd Duke of Grafton","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAugustus_Henry_Fitzroy%2C_3rd_Duke_of_Grafton.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG/500px-Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG/1280px-Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG/500px-Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Woman holding a parapluie at Zenkō-ji, Nagano, Japan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZenkoji-Nagano.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Hatshepsut_temple4_b.jpg